vulnerabilities.suggested_fix:
1) Use balance-delta accounting around collectFees():
   - uint256 b0Before = IERC20(_token0).balanceOf(address(this));
   - uint256 b1Before = IERC20(_token1).balanceOf(address(this));
   - clPool.collectFees();
   - uint256 fees0 = IERC20(_token0).balanceOf(address(this)) - b0Before;
   - uint256 fees1 = IERC20(_token1).balanceOf(address(this)) - b1Before;
   - only forward fees0/fees1.
2) Add access control and/or epoch gating to claimFees() (e.g., onlyDistribution/onlyOwner/onlyGaugeManager) to prevent arbitrary third parties from triggering sweeps.
3) Add a hard safety check: require(rewardToken != token0 && rewardToken != token1) when isForPair, or explicitly exclude rewardToken from fee sweeping.
